ef_epa_per_play":0.1911},{"week":5,"opponent":"MIA","home":false,"pf":31.0,"pa":24.0,"off_snaps":61,"epa_per_play":0.1419,"pass_rate":0.5246,"pass_rate_neutral":0.5676,"def_epa_per_play":-0.03319}],"comps":{"offense":[{"season":2025,"team":"KC","distance":0.4327,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Andy Reid"},{"season":2022,"team":"KC","distance":0.8035,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Andy Reid"},{"season":2024,"team":"KC","distance":0.8052,"shared":12,"play_caller":"Andy Reid"},{"season":2023,"team":"WAS","distance":0.8133,"shared":12,"play_caller":null},{"season":2024,"team":"NYJ","distance":0.8805,"shared":12,"play_caller":null}],"defense":[{"season":2023,"team":"NYJ","distance":0.2353,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Jeff Ulbrich"},{"season":2022,"team":"IND","distance":0.2445,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2025,"team":"LA","distance":0.3357,"shared":4,"play_caller":"Chris Shula"},{"season":2022,"team":"TEN","distance":0.3868,"shared":4,"play_caller":null},{"season":2024,"team":"JAX","distance":0.3907,"shared":4,"play_caller":null}]},"overview":{"overview":"The Bengals are 3-2 through week 6 of the 2026 season and have outscored opponents 128 to 109. The offense ranks 9th in EPA per play and the defense 16th in EPA allowed, so neither side has stood out much yet. Their most distinctive traits are the 3rd highest RPO rate and the lowest blitz rate in the league.","offense":"The Bengals offense has been well above average by EPA per play so far. They have thrown more than almost anyone relative to the situation, even when the score has not called for it. Their biggest outliers in how they line up are the 3rd highest RPO rate and the 2nd highest shotgun rate in the league. Joe Burrow has run the passing game, with Tee Higgins leading the team in targets.","defense":"The Bengals defense has been about average by EPA allowed per play so far. It has been much better against the pass than the run, ranking 8th and 26th. Boye Mafe leads the team with 3 sacks, and Dexter Lawrence has added 3, after not being a regular on this defense last season. In terms of scheme, they have the lowest blitz rate in the league.","special":"The Bengals have been about average in how often they go for it on fourth down. Their kickers have made 100% of field goals, which is the best in the league. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into receivers, about 22% of the money on the books. Their quarterbacks were among the oldest in the league.","players":"Joe Burrow has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 1,361 yards. Tee Higgins has been the clear top target with 23% of the looks and 423 receiving yards. Chase Brown has handled most of the work in the backfield with 72% of the carries. On defense, Boye Mafe leads the team with 3 sacks and Jordan Battle has picked off 3 passes.","coaching":"Zac Taylor is calling the offense as head coach and Al Golden is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2025 and 2022 Chiefs, both under Andy Reid. Their defense looks most like the 2023 Jets under Jeff Ulbrich and the 2022 Colts.","trends":"The offense went from 19th in EPA per play in 2025 to 9th so far this season, a big step forward. The defense moved from 29th in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 16th so far this season, a big step forward.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}